<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Support Desk — parent→school ticketing.

  TRANSLATIONS OUTSTANDING. This app ships five locales (values-hi, -gu, -mr,
  -ta, -te), each with 14 string files. None of them carry these keys yet.
  Android falls back to values/ per-key, so nothing breaks — an untranslated
  string simply appears in English — but a parent using the app in Marathi will
  see an English support screen until a translator supplies the rest.

  One string below is NOT a candidate for casual rewording: support_anon_note.
  "Anonymous" would be a misrepresentation. The reporter's identity IS stored —
  it has to be, or the school cannot reply and abuse cannot be rate-limited.
  The promise being made is narrower: the name is not shown to school staff.
  Say that, and only that.
-->
